  "raw": {
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E21AE295FD7C5DFB0FF43ED6334CDDB0/jobs/394121": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant to the President",
      "description": "Executive Assistant to the President You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Executive Assistant to the President Misenheimer Campus - Misenheimer, NC 28109 Apply Overview Position Type Full-Time Staff Job Shift Day Education Level Bachelor's degree Travel Percentage Up to 50% Category Education Apply Description The Executive Assistant, Office of the President, provides high-level administrative and operational support to the President and designated members of the President’s Cabinet. Reporting to the University President and the Chief of Staff, this position plays a central role in coordinating the day-to-day operations of the President’s Office, supporting executive priorities, facilitating Board of Trustees activities, and ensuring effective communication and follow-through across senior leadership. The Executive Assistant serves as a trusted administrative partner to university leadership and works with a high degree of discretion, judgment, responsiveness, and confidentiality. Full-time, 12 month, Exempt position Duties and Responsibilities: • Provide high-level administrative support to the President and designated Cabinet members, as assigned by the President and Chief of Staff. • Manage complex calendars, meeting schedules, travel arrangements, itineraries, related events, and executive logistics. • Coordinate the day-to-day administrative operations of the Office of the President. • Serve as an administrative liaison among the President, Chief of Staff, Cabinet members, Board of Trustees, and internal and external constituents. • Prepare meeting materials, agendas, briefing documents, presentations, correspondence, and follow-up items for senior leaders. • Coordinate and track action items and priorities arising from Cabinet and other executive-level meetings. • Support the administrative coordination of Board of Trustees meetings, committee meetings, materials, records, minutes, communications, and manage board relations. • Coordinate executive participation in university events, donor engagements, community activities, and other institutional functions. • Support special projects and institutional initiatives led by the President, Chief of Staff, or Cabinet. • Coordinate executive office budgets, purchasing, and routine administrative processes in partnership with the appropriate university departments. • Maintain confidential executive records and information with discretion. • Perform other duties consistent with executive-level administrative support and the responsibilities of the Office of the President. Coordinate the operations and administrative functions of the President’s Office and serve as liaison between the President and the internal and external constituencies of the University; • Serve as liaison between president/university and various higher education and/or Methodist organizations (NCICU, GBGM, NASCUMC, CIC, UMHEF, etc.); • Understands – and is continuously learning how to – leverage technology for the efficient operation of the university, from basic (Microsoft) platforms used university-wide for communication and calendaring, Blackbaud/Raiser’s Edge to improve the president’s participation in Pfeiffer’s fund-raising and friend-raising operations, to emerging technologies and platforms that will maximize efficiency and the office’s ability to prioritize action items. • Perform other duties as assigned. Supervisory Responsibilities: May include supervision of student workers. Work Environment: Position may occasionally require evening or weekend duty. Ability to multitask and prioritize in a fast-paced environment is crucial. Incumbent must exercise tact, diplomacy, confidentiality, and discernment in communicating with internal and external constituents. Minimal local travel required. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required, along with five to six years of experience working in the office of an executive officer. Knowledge, skills, and abilities: • Knowledge and understanding of Board Relations and associated functions required • High level of confidentiality regarding correspondence, conversations, and documents required • Knowledge of higher education administration strongly preferred • Ability to work with varied constituents • Ability to manage multiple tasks simultaneously • Excellent writing skills required • Strong interpersonal and communication skills and the ability to work within a diverse community • Advanced knowledge of computer software, including Microsoft Office suite • Ability to work independently Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E21AE295FD7C5DFB0FF43ED6334CDDB0/jobs/393932": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Business",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Business You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Misenheimer Campus - Misenheimer, NC 28109 Apply Overview Position Type Faculty Job Shift Day Education Level Master's Degree Travel Percentage Travel required Category Education Apply Description PURPOSE: Pfeiffer University invites applications for an Assistant/Associate Professor of Business with a focus in economics and finance. This position offers the opportunity to join a collaborative academic community and help prepare students for meaningful careers through teaching, advising, and mentoring. Teaching responsibilities are primarily in the undergraduate business program and may include economics, finance, and other business courses appropriate to the faculty member’s expertise, delivered through in-person and online modalities. When appropriately credentialed and qualified, and based on workload, the faculty member may also teach in graduate business programs and contribute to the continued development of Pfeiffer’s business offerings. Full-time, 9-month position DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: An asterisk (*) designates an essential function, performed with or without reasonable accommodation. *Teach up to 26 instructional units (IUs) during the academic year, primarily in undergraduate economics, finance, and related business courses consistent with academic credentials and departmental needs. *Develop and deliver course content, learning activities, and assessments that support established learning outcomes, connect disciplinary concepts to practical applications, and provide students with timely, constructive feedback. *Advise and mentor undergraduate business students through regular meetings and ongoing communication to support academic planning, degree progress, and career preparation. *Collaborate with the Department Chair, program coordinator, and business faculty on course scheduling, curriculum development, program assessment, and continuous improvement, including work supporting ACBSP accreditation. *Teach undergraduate business courses across modalities as assigned, using appropriate instructional technologies and practices that support student engagement and achievement. Participate in departmental and University service, program-related campus activities, and community outreach. Contribute to grant development and related initiatives as appropriate. Perform other reasonably related duties consistent with the faculty appointment. The position is based at the Misenheimer campus and involves regular in-person teaching, student advising, and collaboration with Business Department faculty. Teaching assignments may also include online undergraduate courses and graduate business courses, depending on qualifications and departmental needs. Work occurs in classroom, office, and online instructional settings. Responsibilities follow the academic calendar, with recurring deadlines for course preparation, grading, advising, and assessment. The faculty member is expected to respond constructively to changes in course assignments, instructional technology, curriculum, and student needs. BENEFITS: Paid Life Insurance Paid Long Term Disability Tuition Remission and Tuition Exchange Medical, Dental and Vision Insurance 403b Retirement Critical, Accident and Hospital Indemnity Insurance Qualifications REQUIRED: Master’s degree in economics, finance, or a related field from an institutionally accredited institution. Academic preparation appropriate to teaching undergraduate economics and finance courses. Evidence of successful teaching in higher education. Demonstrated communication skills and a commitment to student learning, advising, and mentoring. Familiarity with instructional technology and learning management systems. PREFERRED: Earned doctorate in economics, finance, or a related field from an institutionally accredited institution. Experience teaching online courses. Pfeiffer University complies with applicable state and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment in every location in which the institution has facilities. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation, and training. Pfeiffer University expressly prohibits any form of workplace harassment based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, or veteran status. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E21AE295FD7C5DFB0FF43ED6334CDDB0/jobs/391932": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Religion; Mariam Coltrane Schramm Endowed Professor of Religion & Christian Education",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Religion; Mariam Coltrane Schramm Endowed Professor of Religion & Christian Education You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant/Associate Professor of Religion; Mariam Coltrane Schramm Endowed Professor of Religion & Christian Education Misenheimer Campus - Misenheimer, NC 28109 Apply Overview Position Type Faculty Job Shift Day Education Level Ph.D. (will consider ABD) Travel Percentage Up to 50% Category Education Apply Description PURPOSE: The Assistant/Associate Professor of Religion advances Pfeiffer University's mission through excellence in teaching, student advising and mentoring, scholarship, and service. The faculty member will teach courses in Religion, Interdisciplinary Studies, and the University's Core/Pathways curriculum and, if appropriately qualified, may also teach courses in another, related discipline. As coordinator of the Religion and Practical Theology program, the faculty member will help shape its future direction through an interdisciplinary approach to the study of religion, faith, and contemporary life. Central to this work will be helping students explore vocation and discern meaningful paths rooted in their faith, interests, and sense of purpose. The faculty member will also foster opportunities for servant leadership and community-engaged learning across the program and the broader University. The faculty member will contribute actively to the intellectual, spiritual, and communal life of the University and help strengthen Pfeiffer's historic and onqoinq relationship with The United Methodist Church. This is a full-time, 9-month position, which starts in August 2027. This position is located on Pfeiffer's campus in Misenheimer, NC. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: The successful candidate will have the following responsibilities: Teach up to 26 IUs during the academic year. Teaching assignments will include courses in: The Religion and Practical Theology major Core/Pathways courses Interdisciplinary Studies major Depending on qualifications, teaching assignments may also include courses in the Humanities program. Advise and mentor students. Participate in shared governance, committee assignments, etc . Recruit new students to the undergraduate major in Religion and Practical Theology Work cooperatively with campus ministries. BENEFITS: Tuition Remission/Tuition Exchange Paid Life and LTD Insurance Medical, Dental, & Vision Insurance Accident, Critical Illness, & Hospital Indemnity 403b Retirement Options Qualifications Required qualification: The candidate will possess a PhD (ABO considered) in one of the fields traditionally associated with theological education (e.g. Theology, Biblical Studies, Church History, Religion and Literature, etc.). Preferred qualification: Qualifications to teach courses in the humanities (ideally, 18 graduate hours in History, Church History, Philosophy or a related field). Preference will given to applicants who are active laypersons in a local United Methodist Church and/or clergy who are elders and deacons in full connection with a United Methodist conference. Outstanding candidates with active standing within another denomination in full communion with the United Methodist tradition may also be considered. Equal Opportunity Employment Statement: Pfeiffer University provides equal employment opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, genetics, or other protected group under State and Federal law. In addition to federal law requirements, Pfeiffer University complies with applicable state and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment in every location in which the institution has facilities. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation, and training. Pfeiffer University expressly prohibits any form of workplace harassment based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, or veteran status. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E21AE295FD7C5DFB0FF43ED6334CDDB0/jobs/391377": {
      "title": "Director of Financial Aid",
      "description": "Director of Financial Aid You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of Financial Aid Misenheimer Campus - Misenheimer, NC 28109 Apply Overview Position Type Full-Time Staff Job Shift Day Education Level Master's Degree Travel Percentage Travel required Category Education Apply Description Pfeiffer University seeks an experienced, student-centered, and strategically minded Director of Financial Aid to lead the University's comprehensive financial aid program. Reporting to the Vice President for Enrollment Management, the Director will provide leadership for the day-to-day administration, compliance, awarding, communication, and continuous improvement of financial aid programs serving undergraduate and graduate students. The Director will serve as a key member of Pfeiffer's enrollment management leadership team and will work closely with Admissions, Student Development, Student Accounts, the Registrar, Finance, academic leadership, and other campus partners to ensure that financial aid supports the University's enrollment, retention, affordability, and student-success objectives. The successful candidate will combine strong technical knowledge of federal and state financial aid regulations with the ability to think strategically about financial aid leveraging, institutional scholarship resources, enrollment goals, student affordability, and net tuition revenue. This is an opportunity for a financial aid professional who wants to have an institution-wide impact and help shape how Pfeiffer uses financial aid as both a student-support resource and a strategic tool. Essential Responsibilities A. Financial Aid Leadership & Administration •    Provide leadership and oversight for the University's comprehensive financial aid operation. •    Administer federal, state, institutional, and private financial aid programs in accordance with applicable regulations and University policies. •    Oversee the complete financial aid cycle, including application processing, verification, awarding, adjustments, disbursement, reconciliation, and annual closeout. •    Establish and maintain effective financial aid policies, procedures, and internal controls. •    Ensure accurate and timely financial aid processing for prospective, newly admitted, and continuing students. •    Oversee financial aid for undergraduate, graduate, online, transfer, adult, and other applicable student populations. •    Monitor financial aid calendars, deadlines, and processing milestones to ensure a positive student experience. B. Strategic Enrollment & Financial Aid Management •    Partner with the Vice President for Enrollment Management and enrollment leadership to develop financial aid strategies that support institutional enrollment goals. •    Develop, evaluate, and refine institutional financial aid and scholarship awarding strategies. •    Analyze financial aid packaging, discounting, scholarship utilization, yield, retention, and enrollment outcomes. •    Provide financial aid data and analysis to support enrollment forecasting, enrollment planning, and institutional decision-making. •    Monitor the impact of financial aid policies on enrollment, student demographics, retention, and net tuition revenue. •    Collaborate with Admissions to develop coordinated approaches to scholarship awarding, financial aid communication, and enrollment conversion. •    Participate in enrollment modeling and scenario planning related to changes in tuition, scholarships, grants, student demographics, and financial aid policies. •    Identify opportunities to improve the University's use of institutional aid while maintaining affordability and supporting long-term financial sustainability. •    Help ensure that financial aid practices reflect Pfeiffer's commitment to access, affordability, and student success. C. Compliance & Regulatory Oversight •    Maintain comprehensive knowledge of federal Title IV regulations and applicable state and institutional financial aid requirements. •    Ensure compliance with federal and state regulations governing financial aid administration. •    Oversee federal verification, professional judgment, satisfactory academic progress, return of Title IV funds, over-awards, loan processing, and other required processes. •    Maintain appropriate institutional policies and procedures in response to changes in federal and state regulations. •    Coordinate required federal and state reporting. •    Prepare for and coordinate financial aid audits, program reviews, and other compliance reviews. •    Maintain appropriate institutional controls and documentation related to financial aid administration. •    Serve as a primary institutional resource on financial aid compliance and regulatory changes. D. Student experience & Financial Aid Counseling •    Establish a financial aid operation characterized by responsiveness, accuracy, accessibility, and exceptional customer service. •    Ensure students and families receive clear, timely, and understandable information about financial aid. •    Develop effective communication strategies that help students understand their financial aid options, requirements, deadlines, and responsibilities. •    Serve as a resource for complex financial aid cases and appeals. •    Develop processes that reduce barriers and improve the student experience from admission through enrollment with continued persistence. •    Collaborate with Admissions and Student Development to ensure students experience a seamless transition from recruitment through enrollment and beyond. E. Technology, Data, & Process Improvement •    Provide leadership for the effective use and continuous improvement of the University's financial aid technology and systems, including the University's current financial aid portal and related systems. •    Evaluate financial aid processes for efficiency, accuracy, automation, and student usability. •    Use data and reporting to identify trends, operational issues, and opportunities for improvement. •    Develop dashboards, reports, and other analytical tools that support enrollment management and financial aid decision-making. •    Partner with Information Technology and other campus offices on system enhancements, integrations, testing, and implementation. •    Lead process-improvement initiatives that modernize financial aid operations and improve service to students and families. F. Leadership & Collaboration •    Supervise, develop, and evaluate financial aid staff. •    Establish clear performance expectations and promote a culture of accountability, collaboration, and service. •    Provide professional development and training related to regulatory changes, technology, financial aid practices, and customer service. •    Build strong working relationships across Enrollment Management, Finance, Student Development, Academic Affairs, Information Technology, and other University offices. •    Serve as a collaborative institutional partner and contribute to University-wide enrollment and student ­success initiatives. •    Represent Financial Aid in appropriate campus committees, meetings, and professional organizations. •    Other duties as assigned by the Vice President for Enrollment Management. Benefits: Tuition Remission/Tuition Exchange Paid Life and LTD Insurance Accident, Critical Illness & Hospital Indemnity Insurances Medical, Dental & Vision Insurance 403 b Retirement Plan Options Qualifications A. Minimum Qualifications •    Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution. •    At least 5-7 years of progressively responsible experience in higher education financial aid, preferably including supervisory or leadership experience. •    Demonstrated knowledge of federal Title IV financial aid programs and regulations. •    Experience administering federal, state, institutional, and private financial aid programs. •    Experience with financial aid systems and technology. •    Strong analytical, organizational, communication, and problem-solving skills. •    Demonstrated ability to interpret complex regulations and translate them into effective institutional policies and practices. •    Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet critical regulatory and enrollment deadlines. •    Demonstrated commitment to providing excellent service to students and families. •    Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, administrators, students, and families. B. Preferred Qualifications •    Master's degree in higher education administration, business administration, student affairs, or a related field. •    Seven or more years of progressively responsible financial aid experience. •    Previous experience as a Director, Associate Director, or comparable financial aid leadership role. •    Experience at a small private college or university. •    Experience working within a strategic enrollment management environment. •    Experience with financial aid leveraging, scholarship strategy, or enrollment modeling. •    Experience analyzing financial aid and enrollment data to inform institutional decision-making. •    Experience with PowerFaids or comparable financial aid management systems. •    Experience with Jenzabar or other higher education ERP systems. •    Experience leading financial aid system implementations, upgrades, or process-improvement initiatives. •    Experience with federal and state financial aid audits or program reviews. •    Experience administering institutional scholarships and/or endowed scholarship programs. Equal Opportunity Employment Statement: Pfeiffer University provides equal employment opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, genetics, or other protected group under State and Federal law. In addition to federal law requirements, Pfeiffer University complies with applicable state and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment in every location in which the institution has facilities. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation, and training. Pfeiffer University expressly prohibits any form of workplace harassment based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, or veteran status. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E21AE295FD7C5DFB0FF43ED6334CDDB0/jobs/376013": {
      "title": "Graduate Programs Coordinator",
      "description": "Graduate Programs Coordinator You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Graduate Programs Coordinator Albemarle Campus - Albemarle, NC 28001 Apply Overview Position Type Full-Time Staff Job Shift Day Education Level Bachelor's degree Travel Percentage Travel required Category Education Apply Description Pfeiffer University seeks a relationship-driven and results-oriented Graduate Programs Coordinator to recruit, advise, and enroll prospective graduate students. The Graduate Programs Coordinator serves as the primary point of contact for assigned graduate programs, guiding prospective students through the enrollment process from inquiry to matriculation. This position is responsible for: Developing recruitment partnerships, Managing a prospective student pipeline, Evaluating applications, and Executing enrollment strategies that support institutional growth. The successful candidate will demonstrate strong communication skills, a commitment to student success, and the ability to build meaningful relationships with prospective students, employers, academic partners, and community organizations. Benefits: Paid Life and LTD Insurance Tuition Remission Tuition Exchange Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Voluntary Life Insurance Accident, Critical Illness, and Hospital Indemnity Insurance Retirement Qualifications Bachelor's degree required; Master's degree preferred One to three years of admissions, enrollment management, recruitment, sales, advising, customer service, or relationship-building experience preferred Experience working with adult learners, graduate students, or professional populations is desirable Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities •    Exceptional interpersonal, presentation, and communication skills •    Ability to build and maintain relationships with diverse stakeholders •    Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines •    Experience utilizing CRM systems, databases, and technology tools to manage recruitment activities •    Ability to analyze recruitment data and recommend strategies for continuous improvement •    Demonstrated initiative, adaptability, and problem-solving skills •    Commitment to providing outstanding student-centered service •    Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
