    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E21AE295FD7C5DFB0FF43ED6334CDDB0/jobs/84344": {
      "title": "Adjunct Clinical Nursing Faculty NURS322",
      "description": "Adjunct Clinical Nursing Faculty NURS322 You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Clinical Nursing Faculty NURS322 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Job Shift Day Education Level Bachelor's degree Travel Percentage Travel required Category Education Apply Description Adjunct clinical faculty in maternal child and pediatric nursing, spring semester 2023. Adjunct faculty will take students into maternal child and pediatric settings to provide clinical instruction.  No supervisory responsibilities. Clinical courses are taught in a variety of area hospitals and community organizations. Individual may come to Misenheimer campus on select occasions to assist with simulations as an alternative to attending the clinical site. Qualifications Bachelor of science degree in nursing required, Will also consider an entry level master's degree. Master's degree preferred. Registered nurse with a minimum of two years in clinical practice and hold a current unrestricted license to practice as a registered nurse in North Carolina required. Must meet the qualifications for faculty required by the NC Board of Nursing (www.ncbon.org) within three years of employment. Nurse Educator Certification (CNE) preferred, but all qualified applicants will be considered. Preference is given to applicants with teaching experience. Documented experience and expertise in clinical nursing area relevant to course needs. Provide evidence of license, immunizations, HIPAA, OSHA, CPR or other clinical facility requirements. Valid NC driver's license. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
