    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E21AE295FD7C5DFB0FF43ED6334CDDB0/jobs/28030": {
      "title": "Adjunct - OT",
      "description": "Adjunct - OT You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct - OT Misenheimer Campus - Misenheimer, NC 28109 Apply Overview Level Experienced Position Type Adjunct Travel Percentage None Category Professional Services Apply Description Pfeiffer University seeks qualified candidates to fill the role of Occupational Therapy Adjunct Faculty- for the Occupational Therapy Graduate Program. The position is a part-time appointment to meet course content criteria. The successful candidate will collaborate with teaching, advising, conducting research and experiential learning experiences. The Occupational Therapy Faculty is expected to support the overall mission and vision of Pfeiffer University through excellence in teaching and advising students. A commitment to the principles of servant leadership, working with Graduate/Adult students and involvement in university and community service is required. Contract to be established based on area of expertise and curriculum needs. Responsibilities include: Teaching in area of expertise for variety of courses (technology, hand therapy, assessment and intervention labs for pediatric, adults, anatomy, and kinesiology) Contribute to curricular content Supervising Graduate research projects Active participation in student advisement and service to the University, community and profession. Under the direction of the program director, perform academic responsibilities to fulfill compliance with ACOTE requirements. Develop and maintain scholarship agendas in program, college and community As permitted, participate in international partnerships Participate in service and leadership agendas in program, college and community Occupational therapy students in experiential learning settings and classroom lecture/lab. Mentor other faculty in areas of strengths; assist with orientation of newer faculty. The Occupational Therapy is a new program. Pfeiffer University is a private comprehensive university affiliated with the United Methodist Church known both for a distinctive undergraduate residential experience and for an outstanding array of graduate, undergraduate and continuing education offerings for professional adults. The Health Administration programs are offered at locations in Charlotte, Raleigh and various other cities throughout North Carolina. The innovative delivery approach requires faculty with a commitment to student engagement. The Occupational Therapy program will be in the newly constructed facility along with Physician Assistant program with state of the art simulation hospital/lab and cadaver lab. Interprofessional simulations will be conducted with various disciplines (Nursing, Physician Assistant, Marriage Family Counselors, etc.). Qualifications Earned doctorate (PhD, EdD, DSc, OTD) from an accredited institution or terminal degree appropriate for discipline. NBCOT certification and eligible for NC licensure Minimum of 5 years of clinical experience Teaching experience in higher education and online curricula. Expertise in ( technology, hand therapy, assessment and intervention labs for pediatric and/or adults and anatomy and kinesiology) Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E21AE295FD7C5DFB0FF43ED6334CDDB0/jobs/12166": {
      "title": "Adjunct -  Criminal Justice/Sociology Instructor",
      "description": "Adjunct -  Criminal Justice/Sociology Instructor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct -  Criminal Justice/Sociology Instructor Misenheimer Campus - Misenheimer, NC 28109 Apply Overview Level Experienced Education Level Master's Degree Travel Percentage None Apply Position Description Pfeiffer University is seeking an adjunct for Criminal Justice/Sociology to teach for the Fall semester on the Misenheimer campus. Responsibilities include teaching and advising undergraduate students, participating in curriculum/program development; delivering instruction through a combination of day, evening, and online classes on both the Misenheimer and Charlotte campuses. Pfeiffer University is a private, Liberal Arts University, affiliated with the United Methodist Church, whose mission is to prepare servant leaders for life-long learning. The main campus is located in Misenheimer, approximately 40 miles northeast of Charlotte, NC, with additional locations in Charlotte and the Raleigh area. Position Qualifications Applicants must have a Masters and experience in teaching college-level Criminal Justice/Sociology. Ph.D. preferred (ABD considered). Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E21AE295FD7C5DFB0FF43ED6334CDDB0/jobs/397255": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Admissions Counselor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Admissions Counselor Misenheimer Campus - Misenheimer, NC 28109 Apply Overview Position Type Full-Time Staff Job Shift Day Education Level Bachelor's degree Travel Percentage Travel required Category Education Apply Description To serve the undergraduate admission office as an admissions counselor and participate as part of the overall Enrollment team. Recruit students, perform counseling, external outreach and application review are all significant functions of this position.  This position will serve as a key team member of the admissions department and represent Pfeiffer in a positive manner at all times. Full Time, 12 month Represent the University on and off campus to prospective students, parents, secondary school counselors and other individuals or organizations involved in the college selection process Attend local and regional college fairs and high schools Plan and implement recruitment activities for assigned high schools and territories, including travel in assigned territories Counsel prospective applicants on the admissions process and opportunities at the University Conduct one-on-one admissions counseling sessions via in person appointments, phone calls, emails and texts Review files submitted by applicants for the purposes of making admissions decisions Execute the prescribed communication plan by assigned student groups Will work in a team atmosphere to work towards meeting/exceeding enrollment goals, to craft and tell the Pfeiffer story and to offer co-worker support during peak season when time permits. Other duties as assigned Benefits: Paid LTD and Life Insurance Tuition Remission and Tuition Exchange Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Critical Illness, Short-Term, Accident, and Supplemental Life Insurances 403b Retirement Plan Qualifications Bachelor's degree required Ability to travel to various location with some light lifting to load and transport admission materials, displays and other equipment Some evening and weekend hours required, especially during travel season Strong cross-cultural interpersonal and writing skills are necessary, including public speaking skills and the ability to present the University in a positive way to diverse populations Ability to represent Pfeiffer University and the admissions profession positively Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E21AE295FD7C5DFB0FF43ED6334CDDB0/jobs/397251": {
      "title": "Transfer Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Transfer Admissions Counselor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Transfer Admissions Counselor Misenheimer Campus - Misenheimer, NC 28109 Apply Overview Position Type Full-Time Staff Job Shift Day Education Level Bachelor's degree Travel Percentage Travel required Category Education Apply Description To serve the undergraduate admissions office as an admissions counselor and participate as part of the overall Enrollment team.  Recruit students, perform counseling, external outreach and application review are all significant functions of this position. This position will serve as a key team member of the admissions department and represent Pfeiffer in a positive manner at all times. This is a full-time, 12-month, exempt, staff position. Duties and Responsibilities: Represent the University both on and off campus to prospective students, parents, secondary school counselors and other individuals or organizations involved in the college selection process. Attend college fairs and high school visits Plan and implement recruitment activities for assigned high schools and territories, including travel in assigned territories. Counsel prospective applicants on the admissions process and opportunities at the University. One-on-one admissions counseling.  Admissions counseling occurs primarily by in-person appointments, phone calls, emails and texts. Review files submitted by applicants for the purposes of making admission decisions. Manage ongoing strategic communications. Territory includes Central North Carolina. Other duties as assigned. Expectation of 60 students per academic year. Benefits: Paid LTD and Life Insurance Tuition Remission and Tuition Exchange 403b Retirement Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurances Critical Illness, Accident, Short-Term Disability, and Supplemental Life Insurances Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. This position requires the ability to travel to various locations and to load and transport admissions materials, displays and other equipment. Some evening and weekend hours required, especially during the travel season. Strong cross-cultural interpersonal and writing skills are necessary, including public speaking skills and the ability to present the University in a positive way to diverse populations. Ability to represent Pfeiffer University and the admissions profession positively through a strong, student centered ethic. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
